{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3060","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3060","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3060\",\"parent_revision\":\"13acbe51317903b175f86c4359bb9e4ebe2a3aeda819ffd6d3f1a5f01d1b5f8a\",\"root_revision\":\"13acbe51317903b175f86c4359bb9e4ebe2a3aeda819ffd6d3f1a5f01d1b5f8a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe runtime strings that tell an agent what to call next steer it away from paginated navigation. The compact response's hint recommends loading full content as its first suggestion. The over-budget response tells a caller to request sections individually \u2014 advice a caller who already narrowed to one oversized section has exhausted. Neither mentions the paginated navigation parameters.\\n\\nAgents follow these strings. Documentation is a weaker lever: these are read on every call, at the moment of the decision.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] No hint recommends retrieving everything as its first suggestion, per R7\\n- [ ] The over-budget hint offers an action a narrowed caller has not already taken\\n- [ ] Hints name only mechanisms present in the response they accompany\\n- [ ] Addresses appearing in a hint are valid in that same response\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Priority**: P1 \u2014 small change, disproportionate effect on agent behaviour\\n- Intended behaviour is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`. Component ownership is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/component-architecture.md`. Parent: #3054.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"55800055affee74ec6ed259bacee9c16d154a76e1435a88def7e5c62698cef47\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPvdlPg\"}"}